                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "520f2c50-d6ed-352c-8b8f-bd64a5997d1b",
                        "entry_id": "ecc95641-e475-33d0-9fc9-7f2276306a93",
                        "glosses": [
                            "niet fraai"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "6feeba57-da80-4c14-82d0-19d59a06cc5c",
                                "sense_id": "520f2c50-d6ed-352c-8b8f-bd64a5997d1b",
                                "text": "'Ik begrijp dat De Hoop Scheffer in de etalage ligt, maar de gang van zaken is onelegant en onfatsoenlijk.' Bolkestein werd door het kabinet in 2005 benoemd als overheidscommissaris bij Air France-KLM. Zijn laatste optreden was op 7 juli en tot zijn onvrede wordt hij nu opgevolgd door De Hoop Scheffer, die jaren fractievoorzitter was van Atsma."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3ae545f0-a4d9-4bbd-a85f-1d09dacc3fbd",
                                "sense_id": "520f2c50-d6ed-352c-8b8f-bd64a5997d1b",
                                "text": "Het opmerkelijk hoeveel stijlopties Apple biedt. Het bedrijf staat normaal juist bekend om zijn beperkte aanbod: iPhones zijn in slecht drie kleuren verkrijgbaar, terwijl de iPad maar in twee kleuren te koop is. De keuzevrijheid bij de Apple Watch geeft aan dat het bedrijf vooral op stijl inzet. De meest gehoorde kritiek op veel van de vroege smartwatches zoals de Pebble of de eerste Android-horloges was dat het lelijke vierkantjes waren met onelegante rubberen polsbandjes."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f6538d03-0ada-4091-bd6a-086557240a1a",
                        "source_entry_id": "ecc95641-e475-33d0-9fc9-7f2276306a93",
                        "source_sense_id": "520f2c50-d6ed-352c-8b8f-bd64a5997d1b",
                        "target_lang_word": "graceless",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "graceless",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "65dec6b3-df7c-3467-a5ec-0c94a0defed1",
                                        "entry_id": "b8fa8a17-014e-3dc0-8e97-e5e060dfd463",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Without grace."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7e947a98-759c-4b55-82c3-f93a7879aded",
                                                "sense_id": "65dec6b3-df7c-3467-a5ec-0c94a0defed1",
                                                "text": "Such dutie as the ſubject owes the Prince, / Euen ſuch a woman oweth to her husband: / And when ſhe is froward, peeuiſh, ſullen, ſowre, / And not obedient to his honeſt will, / What is ſhe but a foule contending Rebell / And graceleſſe Traitor to her louing Lord?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3406acb4-9ee0-418f-ae03-ab3f90e47d33",
                                                "sense_id": "65dec6b3-df7c-3467-a5ec-0c94a0defed1",
                                                "text": "For Modes of Faith let graceleſs Zealots fight; / His can't be wrong whoſe Life is in the right."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0b76b342-d33b-4156-9b83-32160e916cb5",
                                                "sense_id": "65dec6b3-df7c-3467-a5ec-0c94a0defed1",
                                                "text": "Not by one measure mayst thou mete our love; / For how should I be loved as I love thee? — / I, graceless, joyless, lacking absolutely / All gifts that with thy queenship best behove; — […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a9112f2f-9b12-4fd2-b477-8ef9f5420e4d",
                                                "sense_id": "65dec6b3-df7c-3467-a5ec-0c94a0defed1",
                                                "text": "There was dancing now on the canvas in the garden; old men pushing young girls backward in eternal graceless circles, superior couples holding each other tortuously, fashionably and keeping in the corners— […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "134e8b0d-9c73-4657-9dbb-471ce7460c09",
                                                "sense_id": "65dec6b3-df7c-3467-a5ec-0c94a0defed1",
                                                "text": "Current toys are made of a graceless material, the product of chemistry, not of nature."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5e9cfdd7-c5f7-41b9-9b8f-b914a81c3930",
                                                "sense_id": "65dec6b3-df7c-3467-a5ec-0c94a0defed1",
                                                "text": "1995, Susan Sontag, \"The Art of Fiction No. 143,\" Interview with Edward Hirsch published in The Paris Review, No. 137, Winter, 1995, p. 7,\n[Hirsch:] Do you mind being called an intellectual? [Sontag:] Well, one never likes to be called anything. […] I suppose there will always be a presumption of graceless oddity—especially if one is a woman."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "94823fe2-9753-3a4a-bcd2-9896d4bb9ee1",
                                        "entry_id": "b8fa8a17-014e-3dc0-8e97-e5e060dfd463",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Lacking gracefulness."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e4898d64-ab9c-408b-9f8f-0ec21d117081",
                                                "sense_id": "94823fe2-9753-3a4a-bcd2-9896d4bb9ee1",
                                                "text": "The boy sketched his roughhewn young contadino just in from the fields, naked except for his brache, kneeling to take off his clodhoppers; the flesh tones a sunburned amber, the figure clumsy, with graceless bumpkin muscles; but the face transfused with light as the young lad gazed up at John."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "18df14c3-65be-3c7b-836a-158d67bf7c13",
                                        "entry_id": "b8fa8a17-014e-3dc0-8e97-e5e060dfd463",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Without the grace of God."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "129452d8-f7be-4b5a-9668-510c32f67b15",
                                                "sense_id": "18df14c3-65be-3c7b-836a-158d67bf7c13",
                                                "text": "For it was approaching that uncanny time of year, the festival of Beltane, when the auld pagans were wont to sacrifice to their god Baal. In this season warlocks and carlines have a special dispensation to do evil, and Alison waited on its coming with graceless joy."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6b61bb36-6252-362a-9c3d-dbeb1bff1e37",
                                        "entry_id": "b8fa8a17-014e-3dc0-8e97-e5e060dfd463",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Unfortunate."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0d338e75-71ed-42ec-9ecd-d68759079947",
                                                "sense_id": "6b61bb36-6252-362a-9c3d-dbeb1bff1e37",
                                                "text": "Much was he grieued with that graceleſſe chaunce, / Yet from the wound no drop of bloud there fell, / But wondrous paine, that did the more enhaunce / His haughtie courage to aduengement fell: / Smart daunts not mighty harts, but makes them more to ſwell."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d32c0d1c-3142-45c3-a5bf-50a518bd01ac",
                        "source_entry_id": "ecc95641-e475-33d0-9fc9-7f2276306a93",
                        "source_sense_id": "520f2c50-d6ed-352c-8b8f-bd64a5997d1b",
                        "target_lang_word": "plump",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "plump",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b5251a56-d540-3698-850d-f2596092b538",
                                        "entry_id": "e218758f-3dc7-3d16-8b27-a43f733daf22",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having a full and rounded shape; chubby, somewhat overweight."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fe3b081e-135c-4117-bb00-96902ee9bbbe",
                                                "sense_id": "b5251a56-d540-3698-850d-f2596092b538",
                                                "text": "a plump baby; plump cheeks"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "559264cb-1c1b-448f-8559-b22bccf41733",
                                                "sense_id": "b5251a56-d540-3698-850d-f2596092b538",
                                                "text": "The god of wine did his plump clusters bring."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eb3576e7-ae6b-4cc6-90ab-e0bd0931cb12",
                                                "sense_id": "b5251a56-d540-3698-850d-f2596092b538",
                                                "text": "My ideal is to be idle and to love a plump girl."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0179ee05-0123-4bbd-b52d-10fe3e29e3ec",
                                                "sense_id": "b5251a56-d540-3698-850d-f2596092b538",
                                                "text": "He was a plump little man and we had been walking uphill at a pace—set by him—far too rapid for his short legs. He breathed stertorously, and half the drops which glimmered on his rotund face were not rain but sweat."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "adc89588-11f3-3267-bd2d-898f809d40b5",
                                        "entry_id": "e218758f-3dc7-3d16-8b27-a43f733daf22",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Fat."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1145c90b-0ea2-325c-b907-8956a92b805f",
                                        "entry_id": "e218758f-3dc7-3d16-8b27-a43f733daf22",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Sudden and without reservation; blunt; direct; downright."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "40352c9b-ec88-4c0e-8b03-ac0b0d2a4670",
                                                "sense_id": "1145c90b-0ea2-325c-b907-8956a92b805f",
                                                "text": "After the plump statement that the author was at Erceldoune and spake with Thomas."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "50866823-4853-4a52-8c43-38d900e2cdaa",
                                                "sense_id": "1145c90b-0ea2-325c-b907-8956a92b805f",
                                                "text": "I've said so haven't I? Plump and plain."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "plump",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f805b283-799c-3b81-bfd7-3aa7ac27f506",
                                        "entry_id": "9b79f342-bb1f-3c25-9c53-17d17f54aec3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To grow plump; to swell out."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
